The gnome warlock Fizzlebang crouched behind a boulder in Stranglethorn, his imp scorching a panting jungle troll. "Go, my darling—*distract* him!" he whispered. The Succubus stepped forth, hips swaying, eyes like liquid shadow. *"Seduce...*" she purred, her voice weaving a spell far older than Elune. The troll’s axe faltered; his eyes glazed. For three dizzy seconds, he forgot to swing. Fizzlebang’s curses tore through his guard. The kill was clean, quick. But as the body fell, the Succubus sighed, fading into mist. "Such *fragile* minds," she murmured, reappearing at his side, her presence a whisper of shame and power. "They stare... always staring. Mortals notice."

**Answer:** *Seduction* causes the target to become charmed briefly after the Succubus kills it, making the corpse visibly glow and drawing unwanted player attention—risking tag theft or PvP. Voidwalkers are silent, invisible to others, and never cause this visual effect, so warlocks avoid the hassle even if Succubus DPS is higher. [end of text]


